The statistical preference for negative residual energy is clearly evident in our observations. The residual energy becomes more negative as the spectral indices $\alpha_{v}$ and $\alpha_{b}$ diverge, i.e. as the magnetic spectral index steepens. Particularly interesting is the consistent level of residual energy along the line $\alpha_{v} = \alpha_{b}$ throughout the range of observations. ![](images/660f864933b54bc3ad44f21c9db8ef6878ad892e7453631558f67c13e328bcd8.jpg)  
